# Code owners — standard-controls plan efb1e3d1 rev 10, A0.1 (with B1).
#
# BOOTSTRAP: the founder owns EVERY path. The App-key broker runs inside the
# main application process, so any module that process imports (auth, session,
# storage, database, route registration, boot) executes with the same
# environment as the App private keys. Selective file ownership would not
# protect key custody; whole-repository ownership does. This matches the plan's
# temporary bootstrap reviewer: the founder approves agent PRs until a second
# agent App exists and A3 proves one App's approval counts.
#
# Narrowing this file later requires either process isolation of the broker
# (so a smaller, named surface holds the keys) or a reviewed plan revision.
# server/scripts/test-codeowners-coverage.ts enforces coverage in CI.

*                                                    @davidwmcintosh

# The entries below repeat the catch-all on purpose. They name the credential,
# identity, authorization, release and schema boundaries explicitly, so the
# coverage check can prove each one stays founder-owned even if the catch-all
# is ever narrowed.

